coder › Implemented `toc(markdown)` in `src/toc.ts`, added tests in `src/toc.test.ts`, on branch `feat/toc` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/toc.ts` — `toc()` splits on lines, toggles `inFence` on lines whose left-trimmed text starts with ` ``` ` and skips fenced lines; matches ATX headings with `/^ {0,3}(#{1,6}) (.*)$/`, takes `level` from the `#` count and `text` as the rest trimmed of surrounding whitespace; builds `slug` by lowercasing `text`, replacing each run of non-letter/digit chars with one `-` (Unicode-aware `[^\\p{L}\\p{N}]+/gu`) and trimming `-` from both ends; dedups with a global used-set plus per-base counter, appending `-2`, `-3`, … and skipping taken `-N` slugs.
- `src/toc.test.ts` — 9 tests: heading levels/text/slugs, 1–6 levels plus whitespace trim, non-headings (`#######`, `#No space`, plain text) ignored, fenced blocks ignored, slug punctuation/unicode handling, dash trimming, `-2/-3` duplicates incl. colliding slug bases (`Hello World` vs `Hello-World`), taken-`-2` skip, empty input.

