Decisions the task did not spell out:
- Allowed up to 3 leading spaces before `#` (CommonMark allows indented ATX headings); otherwise strict: 1–6 `#` then exactly one space required before text.
- A fence is any line whose left-trimmed text starts with ` ``` ` (so ` ```js ` opens/closes); fence marker lines themselves are never headings.
- Slug char class is Unicode letters/digits, so e.g. `Café` → `café-au-lait` rather than `caf-au-lait`.
- Headings with empty text after trim produce an empty slug, which still participates in dedup (`""`, `"-2"`, …).

